 "consolidated_verdicts": {
  "headline": "NO cap in Lane A3 is board-movement/display compression - all five are input guards / a shrink hyperparameter / a safety floor. NONE should be removed for accuracy. The ONE actionable accuracy lever is the reliability shrink K: the shipped 100/80 OVER-shrinks; loosening to 50/40 lifts OOS (pit rho +0.0034) without lowering Spearman OR AUC on either side.",
  "age_rel_level_clamp_3.5": {
   "classification": "NUMERICAL-SAFETY (linear-feature over-extrapolation guard; NOT display/board compression)",
   "load_bearing_for_accuracy": "weak (hit side)",
   "recommendation": "KEEP",
   "evidence": "removing the clamp LOWERS hit OOS (rho 0.3787->0.3768, dSp -0.00197, dAUC -0.00042) and is ~neutral on pit (rho 0.302->0.3017, dSp -0.00033); both CI-neutral. Loosening to +/-5 or +/-7 is OOS-identical to uncapped (no OOS row exceeds |5|), so the clamp only touches the >3.5 tail. Removal fails the program gate (must not LOWER OOS) on hit.",
   "optional_loosen": "if maximal true-to-model is wanted, +/-5 is OOS-identical to uncapped and still guards |>5| cameos",
   "touches": "efv_dataset._milb_features (age_rel clamp) - DIFF-ONLY (not owned)"
  },
  "reliability_shrink_K": {
   "classification": "HYPERPARAMETER (shrink strength) + numerical-safety (cameo-blowup guard)",
   "load_bearing_for_accuracy": "YES - direction is load-bearing (higher K measurably worse); shipped value is SUBOPTIMAL (too much shrink)",
   "recommendation": "LOOSEN to K_REL_PA=50 / K_REL_BF=40 (x0.5)",
   "evidence": "K_x0.5: hit dSp 0.00052 / dAUC 0.00075 (rho 0.3787->0.3792); pit dSp 0.0034 / dAUC 0.00021 (rho 0.302->0.3055). ALL FOUR deltas non-negative -> clears the 'does not lower OOS' gate. K=0 (no shrink) gives the hit max (rho 0.3815) but HURTS pit AUC (dAUC -0.00372) and strips the cameo guard -> NOT recommended. RAISING K is measurably worse (pit K_x2 rho 0.302->0.2987, dSp -0.00332). CI-neutral (lo95<0) so flagged owner-decision under the strict lo95>0 bar, but point + monotonicity + AUC-safety all favor the loosen.",
